course: dictionary
lesson: 7269
title: Pillow: a soft word with many uses
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pillow is a soft bag, usually filled with feathers, foam or cotton, that you rest your head on in bed. You can work out its meaning from the words around it. «Maeve finds Mam's perfume and sprays it on her pillow; it smells like a hug.» Her head rests on the pillow, so it must be the soft thing she lies on.
explain: Pillow can also mean any soft thing used in the same way. Words like pillow fight, pillowcase and fluff the pillow show you the everyday use. Children have pillow fights at sleepovers and change the pillowcase when they wash their bedding.
explain: Pillows also appear in stories and in health advice. In many stories, a child puts a tooth under the pillow for the tooth fairy. Babies sleep without pillows for safety. Always check the sentence around the word to see which sense the writer means.
fact: A pillow is a soft bag you rest your head on in bed.
fact: Pillows are filled with feathers, foam or cotton.
fact: Pillow can be a verb, but it is rare: it means to rest your head on something soft.
fact: Phrases to know: pillow fight, pillowcase, under the pillow, fluff the pillow.
fact: Babies sleep without pillows for safety, and phones should never be charged under a pillow or duvet, because the heat cannot escape.
exercise: «Maeve finds Mam's perfume and sprays it on her pillow; it smells like a hug.» Where does Maeve spray the perfume? | On her hairbrush | On the stairs | In the bath | *On her pillow
exercise: What is a pillowcase? | *A cover that goes over a pillow | A pillow fight | A bag for a school book | A kind of bed
exercise: Why do babies sleep without pillows? | Because pillows are too heavy to carry | To make them cold | *For safety | To help them dream
test: What is a pillow filled with? | Water | *Feathers, foam or cotton | Sand | Stone
test: «Children sometimes put a tooth under the pillow for the tooth fairy.» Where is the tooth kept? | In the sink | In a drawer | *Under the pillow | On the window
exam: «Chargers get warm, so under a pillow or duvet the heat cannot escape.» Why is it unsafe to charge a phone under a pillow? | *The heat cannot escape, and the charger can get very hot | Pillows stop electricity working | The pillow is too soft for the phone | The phone will be too cold to use
